  "detail": "A blocked round runs `gh pr ready --undo` on a ready PR. Approval (`limitless review <run> --approve --sha <head>`) only records the SHA, and the land queue never marks a PR ready, while GitHub refuses to merge drafts. A temporary test confirmed it: after approval the PR stayed a draft with no ready call, and the land entry ended `blocked` with `merge failed`. So the round that existed to make the fix landable leaves the PR unlandable. Fix: leave the PR's draft state unchanged on a round push. The run ending `needs_human` and the evidence comment already tell the owner to verify. (Landing a first delivery's draft PR stays a manual step, the GUIDE's \"mark the PR ready\", and is out of scope here.) Test: a blocked round on a ready PR pushes, comments and makes no `gh pr ready` call."
